Examines practical concurrency design for ordering guarantees under backpressure in a multi-client, multi-document setting, including missing/late edits and dynamic scaling.

## Key Concepts

- Bounded queues and backpressure signaling
- Per-document causal ordering using logical clocks or vector clocks
- Per-document buffers and a scheduler that avoids cross-document reordering
- Dynamic worker scaling and fault-tolerant enqueue/consume paths

